# Lacuna — women's health M&A intelligence platform

See AGENTS.md for full conventions.

## Stack
Next.js 16, React 19, TypeScript (strict), Tailwind CSS v4, D3.js v7, Framer Motion, TensorFlow.js.
HTTP: native `fetch` only (no axios). Data: `getVerifiedDataset()` from `src/data/dataset.verified.json`.

## Project layout
- `src/app/` — pages + API routes (Next.js App Router)
- `src/components/` — React components (PascalCase filenames)
- `src/lib/` — business logic, utilities, adapters
- `src/data/` — verified JSON dataset (single source of truth)
- `@/*` path alias resolves to `src/*`

## Dataset structure
`dataset.verified.json` has three arrays: `companies`, `acquirers`, `acquisitions`.
Every deal links `acquirerId` → `targetId` with public source citations.

## Key rules
- No `async` without `await` (Deno CI fails)
- No synthetic `maDeals` data — only verified dataset
- No invented TAM/SAM, sector-multiple fallbacks, or keyword risk scores in UI — show "insufficient data" instead
- Components ~300 lines max; prefer `interface` for shared shapes
- Commits: `feat:` / `fix:` / `chore:` — short, why-focused

## CI
`npm run lint` (ESLint) + `deno lint` (require-await, no-unused-vars) + Vercel deploy preview
